01:00:58.992 --> 01:00:59.825
- Could you imagine, it's just like?

01:00:59.825 --> 01:01:01.330
(Joey imitates squeaking)

01:01:01.330 --> 01:01:03.170
Hello!
(all chuckling)

01:01:03.170 --> 01:01:06.105
- They used to have a box just
full of really old t-shirts.

01:01:06.105 --> 01:01:07.440
- Really?
- At one of the studio's

01:01:07.440 --> 01:01:08.590
I worked at, and they were just like,

01:01:08.590 --> 01:01:10.300
if you wore anything that wasn't a t-shirt

01:01:10.300 --> 01:01:11.290
they were like, put the t-shirt.

01:01:11.290 --> 01:01:12.130
- Wow.
- Right.

01:01:12.130 --> 01:01:14.130
- That doesn't sound sanitary.

01:01:14.130 --> 01:01:14.963
- Well it was, you know.

01:01:14.963 --> 01:01:16.100
- Just wearing someone's sweaty t-shirt.

01:01:16.100 --> 01:01:17.642
- They washed them.

01:01:17.642 --> 01:01:19.543
But it was just like,

01:01:19.543 --> 01:01:21.420
"Don't bring anything that isn't a t-shirt

01:01:21.420 --> 01:01:22.470
because it makes too much noise."

01:01:22.470 --> 01:01:23.427
- Yeah.
- Makes sense.

01:01:23.427 --> 01:01:25.420
- And like, don't have keys in your pocket

01:01:25.420 --> 01:01:26.253
or anything like that.

01:01:26.253 --> 01:01:27.830
Like just empty your pockets.

01:01:27.830 --> 01:01:28.700
- I'd hate to be that
guy who just like came on

01:01:28.700 --> 01:01:31.311
and was like, "Shit, I
need to sneeze right now."

01:01:31.311 --> 01:01:34.290
(all laughing)

01:01:34.290 --> 01:01:35.130
- And I feel that like,

01:01:35.130 --> 01:01:36.380
the pressure is even greater

01:01:36.380 --> 01:01:39.370
because it's like, if you
fuck up a line for instance,

01:01:39.370 --> 01:01:41.243
then all the actors are
there to kind of like.

01:01:41.243 --> 01:01:43.473
- Yeah, so what happens if
someone flubs their line?

01:01:43.473 --> 01:01:44.640
I mean, that happens.

01:01:44.640 --> 01:01:47.013
- Well, because we're recording, like,

01:01:48.013 --> 01:01:50.840
I think we record like each 15 minutes

01:01:50.840 --> 01:01:52.003
of an anime, if that makes sense?

01:01:52.003 --> 01:01:52.836
- Yeah.

01:01:52.836 --> 01:01:55.980
- So like, if you mess up your line,

01:01:55.980 --> 01:01:59.852
you just stay silent and
just back away and then-

01:01:59.852 --> 01:02:01.340
- Have you ever done that?

01:02:01.340 --> 01:02:03.123
- Yeah.
(boys groaning)

01:02:03.123 --> 01:02:04.736
It's so like, it's like-

01:02:04.736 --> 01:02:07.324
- Stupid, stupid, stupid.

01:02:07.324 --> 01:02:08.975
- I could see like the PTSD in her face

01:02:08.975 --> 01:02:10.520
as she was like telling the story.

01:02:10.520 --> 01:02:12.914
I was like, oh, she
she's experienced this.

01:02:12.914 --> 01:02:14.770
- It's like, if you mess up,

01:02:14.770 --> 01:02:16.670
you can't say like, oops,
or anything like that.

01:02:16.670 --> 01:02:18.470
You just have to like, stay silent

01:02:18.470 --> 01:02:21.320
so the person after you
can say their lines.

01:02:21.320 --> 01:02:22.590
And so like once-
- Oh!

01:02:22.590 --> 01:02:23.938
So they can just like
cut your part, right?

01:02:23.938 --> 01:02:25.146
- Cut it, yeah.
- Oh okay, that makes sense.

01:02:25.146 --> 01:02:26.010
- And then they can take it again

01:02:26.010 --> 01:02:29.030
after the whole 15 minutes
is like recorded, right?

01:02:29.030 --> 01:02:32.620
- Oh yeah.
- So, and it's really hard

01:02:32.620 --> 01:02:34.640
because when you first start voice acting,

01:02:34.640 --> 01:02:36.787
right, the director tells you like,

01:02:36.787 --> 01:02:39.430
"We want that line said
more like this way,"

01:02:39.430 --> 01:02:41.840
or like, "In a different
way to what you did."

01:02:41.840 --> 01:02:44.593
And if you're not like able to like,

01:02:46.030 --> 01:02:48.560
say it like how the director
wants you to say it,

01:02:48.560 --> 01:02:50.370
you like, take it again and again.

01:02:50.370 --> 01:02:51.830
But you're taking it again and again

01:02:51.830 --> 01:02:53.790
right in front of all your senpais.

01:02:53.790 --> 01:02:55.780
So like you're taking their time,

01:02:55.780 --> 01:02:58.073
and the director's like,

01:02:58.073 --> 01:03:00.300
"We want it more like this way."

01:03:00.300 --> 01:03:03.200
And you're like, "Okay, I'll try my best."

01:03:03.200 --> 01:03:04.033
And so, yeah, it's really-

01:03:04.033 --> 01:03:05.300
- That's so nerve-wracking!

01:03:05.300 --> 01:03:07.260
- Oh yeah.
- That's, that's like two,

01:03:07.260 --> 01:03:08.832
that's like pressure on top of pressure.

01:03:08.832 --> 01:03:09.665
- Yeah.
- Right?

01:03:09.665 --> 01:03:11.150
- You're already pressured to be like,

01:03:11.150 --> 01:03:12.440
I'm gonna nail my line

01:03:12.440 --> 01:03:14.170
just so I can put on a good performance.

01:03:14.170 --> 01:03:15.003
- It's sort of like the teacher going,

01:03:15.003 --> 01:03:16.300
all right, what's the answer?

01:03:16.300 --> 01:03:17.700
You, you, you specifically,

01:03:17.700 --> 01:03:19.410
what is the answer to this math question?

01:03:19.410 --> 01:03:20.243
You don't know?

01:03:20.243 --> 01:03:21.351
Come on, you can do it, come on.

01:03:21.351 --> 01:03:22.697
Come on, come on.

01:03:22.697 --> 01:03:25.170
- We'll all wait until
you figure it out, right?

01:03:25.170 --> 01:03:27.272
- Have you ever had the director explain

01:03:27.272 --> 01:03:29.280
how they wanted you to
do the line differently,

01:03:29.280 --> 01:03:30.130
and you're like, what?

01:03:30.130 --> 01:03:31.820
I, that does not make any sense.

01:03:31.820 --> 01:03:36.820
- Yeah, when I was
first, like in an anime,

01:03:36.940 --> 01:03:39.100
one of the directors told me,

01:03:39.100 --> 01:03:40.511
like in Japanese, they said,

01:03:40.511 --> 01:03:42.880
(speaking in Japanese)

01:03:42.880 --> 01:03:43.713
and yeah.

01:03:43.713 --> 01:03:45.287
And I was like, 'cause I was.

01:03:45.287 --> 01:03:46.817
- What does that mean?
- It's like-

01:03:46.817 --> 01:03:47.650
- (speaking in Japanese) is like,

01:03:47.650 --> 01:03:49.716
like soft sword fighting.
- Yeah.

01:03:49.716 --> 01:03:51.730
- Oh, okay?
- With like, yeah.

01:03:51.730 --> 01:03:52.900
So basically like play sword fighting.

01:03:52.900 --> 01:03:53.980
- Yeah, yeah.
- So it's like,

01:03:53.980 --> 01:03:56.303
sound more play sword fighting.

01:03:56.303 --> 01:03:57.136
- That's so specific.
- Yeah.

01:03:57.136 --> 01:03:59.930
And I was like, and at
that time I was like,

01:03:59.930 --> 01:04:01.610
I didn't know the word
(speaking in Japanese).

01:04:01.610 --> 01:04:02.720
(all chuckling)

01:04:02.720 --> 01:04:04.137
- Got you, chief.

01:04:05.083 --> 01:04:08.340
- It would be so awkward
to ask the director,

01:04:08.340 --> 01:04:09.920
what does (speaking in
Japanese) mean, right?

01:04:09.920 --> 01:04:11.530
- Yeah, yeah.
- So I was like,

01:04:12.667 --> 01:04:13.850
"Okay, I'll try my best."

01:04:13.850 --> 01:04:16.350
And so I asked the person
next to me who was around

01:04:16.350 --> 01:04:17.365
the same age as me,
- Yeah.

01:04:17.365 --> 01:04:20.557
- like, what's (speaking in Japanese).

01:04:20.557 --> 01:04:22.430
And she told me and I was like-

01:04:22.430 --> 01:04:23.688
- And it still didn't make any sense.

01:04:23.688 --> 01:04:24.634
- Yeah.

01:04:24.634 --> 01:04:25.922
- What the fuck does that mean?

01:04:25.922 --> 01:04:27.665
- Yeah, yeah.

01:04:27.665 --> 01:04:29.410
- So, what does that mean?

01:04:29.410 --> 01:04:30.390
Like, how did you?

01:04:30.390 --> 01:04:32.090
- Did you find out what he wanted?

01:04:33.373 --> 01:04:34.659
- I'm not sure.
(all laughing)

01:04:34.659 --> 01:04:37.077
- To this day, I've wondered
what the take should've been.

01:04:37.077 --> 01:04:38.510
- But I got an okay.

01:04:38.510 --> 01:04:40.970
So I guess I was able to, you know.

01:04:40.970 --> 01:04:43.183
- Was that an okay or was that like, okay.

01:04:44.212 --> 01:04:45.644
- Oo, oo.
- Right?

01:04:45.644 --> 01:04:46.977
It could be either one, right?
- Yeah.

01:04:46.977 --> 01:04:49.100
- Yeah there's a, when you're doing lines,

01:04:49.100 --> 01:04:50.410
sometimes there's that feeling of like,

01:04:50.410 --> 01:04:52.100
you're not getting it, and then you just,

01:04:52.100 --> 01:04:54.050
you know personally
you're not gonna get it.

01:04:54.050 --> 01:04:56.150
And then they're just
like, "We'll just move on."

01:04:56.150 --> 01:04:57.895
And I'm like, no!
- Yeah.

01:04:57.895 --> 01:04:59.002
- Why, tell me!

01:04:59.002 --> 01:05:00.810
- Yeah, I get that feeling.

01:05:00.810 --> 01:05:05.070
- Have you ever like said a
line that you've just been like,

01:05:05.070 --> 01:05:06.260
that was an awful take.

01:05:06.260 --> 01:05:07.330
And the director's been like, "All right,

01:05:07.330 --> 01:05:08.560
we're moving on, that was a good take."

01:05:08.560 --> 01:05:09.770
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:05:09.770 --> 01:05:12.063
I've had that a lot.
- Okay.

01:05:12.063 --> 01:05:13.510
- That's why I usually say like, fuck,

01:05:13.510 --> 01:05:15.067
at the end of my line if I hated it.

01:05:15.067 --> 01:05:17.117
But then they would tell
you to stop saying fuck,

01:05:17.117 --> 01:05:18.650
because you're ruining
the line that they liked.

01:05:18.650 --> 01:05:20.370
You'd be like, da-da-da-fuck!

01:05:20.370 --> 01:05:21.980
Because then you couldn't use it.

01:05:21.980 --> 01:05:23.460
- Are you the type of voice actor

01:05:23.460 --> 01:05:25.970
that watches the anime that they were in

01:05:25.970 --> 01:05:28.280
after it like finishes
and airs and everything?

01:05:28.280 --> 01:05:29.420
- Yeah.
- To like look back on?

01:05:29.420 --> 01:05:30.497
To kind of learn from?
- Yep.

01:05:30.497 --> 01:05:32.525
- 'Cause I cannot do that.

01:05:32.525 --> 01:05:33.358
- Really?

01:05:33.358 --> 01:05:36.103
- Like I hate hearing
myself in voice acting roles

01:05:36.103 --> 01:05:39.243
because I get kind of secondhand
embarrassment from it.

01:05:39.243 --> 01:05:40.510
- Right, yeah.
- 'Cause I always,

01:05:40.510 --> 01:05:42.060
I'm so harsh on myself all the time.

01:05:42.060 --> 01:05:43.970
So when I hear myself on
like a game or an anime,

01:05:43.970 --> 01:05:45.480
I'm always like, I could
have done that line

01:05:45.480 --> 01:05:46.560
like 10 times better.

01:05:46.560 --> 01:05:47.393
Why did they have to use that one?

01:05:47.393 --> 01:05:48.230
- Yeah, I know how you feel.

01:05:48.230 --> 01:05:49.480
- That's good, though, right?

01:05:49.480 --> 01:05:51.040
Like you know that you could improve.

01:05:51.040 --> 01:05:51.873
- Yeah, yeah.

01:05:51.873 --> 01:05:53.010
- It's good, but it's also like,

01:05:53.010 --> 01:05:54.000
when people tell me being like,

01:05:54.000 --> 01:05:55.710
"Oh, I heard you in the game,"

01:05:55.710 --> 01:05:58.966
then I'd be like, I don't
know how I sound in that.

01:05:58.966 --> 01:06:01.270
So it's like, I can't even
like talk about the role

01:06:01.270 --> 01:06:02.500
that I'm in.
- Yeah.

01:06:02.500 --> 01:06:04.189
- Because I just don't know
how it turned out, right?

01:06:04.189 --> 01:06:06.013
- But there's a lot of
like big anima voice actors

01:06:06.013 --> 01:06:07.740
that are like that, as well.

01:06:07.740 --> 01:06:08.783
- Yeah, yeah, it's like,

01:06:08.783 --> 01:06:11.830
I mean, like hearing your
own voice after it's like,

01:06:11.830 --> 01:06:12.920
'cause like you record it

01:06:12.920 --> 01:06:15.650
and it's aired several
months after you've recorded.

01:06:15.650 --> 01:06:17.840
So obviously like several months after,

01:06:17.840 --> 01:06:18.850
you're kind of like,

01:06:18.850 --> 01:06:20.920
you've like brushed up on
your acting a little bit more

01:06:20.920 --> 01:06:22.930
than what you had before.

01:06:22.930 --> 01:06:25.380
So like hearing again, it's like, oh,

01:06:25.380 --> 01:06:27.852
like I didn't say that line properly.

01:06:27.852 --> 01:06:29.940
And I'm really strict on myself, as well.

01:06:29.940 --> 01:06:33.150
So it's kinda like, I look like (groans),

01:06:33.150 --> 01:06:35.260
but then like I think
it's really important

01:06:35.260 --> 01:06:37.250
to like kind of look back.
- Reflect?

01:06:37.250 --> 01:06:38.083
- Yeah.

01:06:38.083 --> 01:06:40.310
- I think the thing that
everyone always says the most

01:06:40.310 --> 01:06:42.020
when they try and start
voice acting is like,

01:06:42.020 --> 01:06:42.890
they hate their own voice.

01:06:42.890 --> 01:06:43.723
They can't stand it.

01:06:43.723 --> 01:06:45.133
And it's just a thing you have to like,

01:06:45.133 --> 01:06:48.140
I mean, personally, I just
think that if you learn

01:06:48.140 --> 01:06:49.630
to like be able to listen to your voice

01:06:49.630 --> 01:06:52.670
and not just recoil in disgust,

01:06:52.670 --> 01:06:54.540
you can then start breaking
it down and being like,

01:06:54.540 --> 01:06:55.373
okay, I didn't do this that well.

01:06:55.373 --> 01:06:56.910
Right, you can start really focusing

01:06:56.910 --> 01:06:57.797
on what you're doing wrong.

01:06:57.797 --> 01:06:58.630
- But isn't it weird that I'm okay

01:06:58.630 --> 01:07:01.000
with hearing my own
voice in YouTube videos?

01:07:01.000 --> 01:07:01.993
- It's just different.
- Oh, really?

01:07:01.993 --> 01:07:03.259
- It's 'cause you've
heard it so many times.

01:07:03.259 --> 01:07:04.400
- Because when you're acting,

01:07:04.400 --> 01:07:07.250
you're trying to do something
like you're trying to perform.

01:07:07.250 --> 01:07:08.970
- Right.
- But YouTube it's just you.

01:07:08.970 --> 01:07:09.803
- Yeah, yeah.

01:07:09.803 --> 01:07:10.636
- Hi, I'm being me I'm being an idiot.

01:07:10.636 --> 01:07:12.070
- That's true, that's true.
- It's just life.

01:07:12.070 --> 01:07:15.380
- I mean, I feel though in
a lot of my roles, like,

01:07:15.380 --> 01:07:17.481
'cause I'm not trained or
anything like that, right.

01:07:17.481 --> 01:07:18.544
I just do it 'cause I like it

01:07:18.544 --> 01:07:19.540
and I'm given the opportunity.

01:07:19.540 --> 01:07:21.850
But like the "Pop Team
Epic" one, for instance.

01:07:21.850 --> 01:07:25.339
- Yeah.
- I played a New York mayor.

01:07:25.339 --> 01:07:28.484
(all laughing)
- Really?

01:07:28.484 --> 01:07:32.390
- And I cannot do a New York accent.

01:07:32.390 --> 01:07:34.193
So, dead ass if you watch

01:07:34.193 --> 01:07:36.470
like the actual episode that aired,

01:07:36.470 --> 01:07:39.330
it's like the most Aussie-sounding
fucking New York Mayor.

01:07:39.330 --> 01:07:40.163
- It is, it is.

01:07:40.163 --> 01:07:41.430
- I'm the Mayor of New York.

01:07:41.430 --> 01:07:43.490
- I just love that idea
that you did the take

01:07:43.490 --> 01:07:44.760
and the director was like, "It's perfect."

01:07:44.760 --> 01:07:45.593
- Yeah, yeah.

01:07:45.593 --> 01:07:47.120
- You're like, "No,
please, please, please."

01:07:47.120 --> 01:07:47.953
- Yeah, yeah.

01:07:47.953 --> 01:07:49.680
I did it, I did the first take

01:07:49.680 --> 01:07:50.870
just thinking like,

01:07:50.870 --> 01:07:52.280
we're going to kind of get like a gauge

01:07:52.280 --> 01:07:54.727
of like how not good
my New York accent is.

01:07:54.727 --> 01:07:56.623
And I actually gave up halfway.

01:07:56.623 --> 01:07:59.010
I tried to do like an American accent.

01:07:59.010 --> 01:08:00.710
But at that point, especially,

01:08:00.710 --> 01:08:01.970
I was like my New York accent,

01:08:01.970 --> 01:08:03.583
or my American accent is not that good

01:08:03.583 --> 01:08:07.280
where like I can confidently
act in that accent.

01:08:07.280 --> 01:08:08.113
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:08:08.113 --> 01:08:09.600
- Like I can try and
speak casually, right.

01:08:09.600 --> 01:08:11.150
But acting in another accent

01:08:11.150 --> 01:08:13.230
is a completely different set of skills.

01:08:13.230 --> 01:08:16.430
So I was like, I'm just gonna
like subtly turn it off.

01:08:16.430 --> 01:08:19.276
Like just turn the gauge down
as the recording goes on.

01:08:19.276 --> 01:08:23.437
So by the end of it, I was
just like, "Yeah, New York!"

01:08:24.419 --> 01:08:26.890
It was like the most
Australian-sounding New York.

01:08:26.890 --> 01:08:28.436
- Yeah, I remember seeing
that and I was just like,

01:08:28.436 --> 01:08:30.392
I feel like he's about to drop the C-bomb.

01:08:30.392 --> 01:08:32.169
'Cause as an Aussie, when's it coming?

01:08:32.169 --> 01:08:33.889
When's it coming?

01:08:33.889 --> 01:08:36.168
- No, but it was so funny
because like I thought for sure,

01:08:36.168 --> 01:08:38.627
I would get some pointers being like,

01:08:38.627 --> 01:08:39.767
"All right, you started off good,

01:08:39.767 --> 01:08:41.850
but you kind of depleted near the end.

01:08:41.850 --> 01:08:43.975
Let's do another take or like,
let's try that line again,"

01:08:43.975 --> 01:08:44.808
or something like that.

01:08:44.808 --> 01:08:45.710
Fully expecting it.

01:08:45.710 --> 01:08:48.460
The director was like,
"All right, you're good!"

01:08:48.460 --> 01:08:49.710
- Yeah, but the director
didn't speak English, right?

01:08:49.710 --> 01:08:50.580
- No.
- Oh, well, then-

01:08:50.580 --> 01:08:53.349
- So he thought I was like
perfect New Yorker accent.

01:08:53.349 --> 01:08:54.182
It's like, yeah.

01:08:54.182 --> 01:08:55.420
That's that's what all people
in New York sound like.

01:08:55.420 --> 01:08:56.350
- I can't blame him, though,

01:08:56.350 --> 01:08:57.183
because he doesn't know.

01:08:57.183 --> 01:08:58.060
There's no way he'd know, right.

01:08:58.060 --> 01:08:58.893
- Yeah, exactly.

01:08:58.893 --> 01:09:00.370
- But in Japan, it's like,

01:09:00.370 --> 01:09:02.430
when you go to recordings, it's like,

01:09:02.430 --> 01:09:04.100
when you talk in English, it's like,

01:09:04.100 --> 01:09:06.750
they expect you to speak
in an American accent,

01:09:06.750 --> 01:09:08.670
but you know, 'cause
I'm from Australia too.

01:09:08.670 --> 01:09:10.710
So it's like, yeah, I try.

01:09:10.710 --> 01:09:11.940
- You never practiced your American accent

01:09:11.940 --> 01:09:12.970
when you were practicing?

01:09:12.970 --> 01:09:14.680
- Well, yeah, like I'm practicing now.

01:09:14.680 --> 01:09:16.670
- Okay.
- But it's still really hard

01:09:16.670 --> 01:09:19.300
to like, I don't know, like
pronounce all these words.

01:09:19.300 --> 01:09:22.640
- American English goes
everything against Australian.

01:09:22.640 --> 01:09:23.583
- Yeah, yeah, I know.

01:09:23.583 --> 01:09:25.070
I mean, I can't do American accents.

01:09:25.070 --> 01:09:26.796
- We have to like contort our faces

01:09:26.796 --> 01:09:27.654
in ways that we wouldn't.
- Yeah, yeah.

01:09:27.654 --> 01:09:29.993
- Just the rrr sound is so like, ugh.

01:09:29.993 --> 01:09:31.510
- Yeah, like card?

01:09:31.510 --> 01:09:33.000
Card, card?
- Yeah, card.

01:09:33.000 --> 01:09:33.833
Card and--
- Well it like,

01:09:33.833 --> 01:09:35.700
the British Australian English,

01:09:35.700 --> 01:09:38.420
like the tongue is like
towards the front of the mouth

01:09:38.420 --> 01:09:40.403
and in American English it's
like flatter in the back.

01:09:40.403 --> 01:09:42.863
And that's like really hard
to do when you're British,

01:09:42.863 --> 01:09:46.070
because you're like, why do I
have to force my tongue down.

01:09:46.070 --> 01:09:47.785
- You just sound like you're
kind of drowning half the time?

01:09:47.785 --> 01:09:48.676
- Yeah, yeah.

01:09:48.676 --> 01:09:50.470
I think, you know, mine sounds shit.

01:09:50.470 --> 01:09:52.300
Like, I barely can.

01:09:52.300 --> 01:09:54.180
- I mean, I'm much better
at it now since then,

01:09:54.180 --> 01:09:55.890
because I practiced, but I mean,

01:09:55.890 --> 01:09:58.190
I still couldn't confidently do

01:09:58.190 --> 01:10:00.350
like an American English role.

01:10:00.350 --> 01:10:02.060
But I feel like, I don't know,

01:10:02.060 --> 01:10:04.120
just from like watching
the anime recently,

01:10:04.120 --> 01:10:05.933
where like we are starting to get more

01:10:05.933 --> 01:10:09.140
like English speaking roles
done by actual native people.

01:10:09.140 --> 01:10:09.973
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:10:09.973 --> 01:10:11.340
- I feel like I've noticed like,

01:10:11.340 --> 01:10:13.960
I think finally anime
directors and producers

01:10:13.960 --> 01:10:16.772
are like, "Different
accents in English exist."

01:10:16.772 --> 01:10:18.680
- In Japanese dubs or?

01:10:18.680 --> 01:10:20.350
- In Japanese dubs.
- All right.

01:10:20.350 --> 01:10:21.980
- But even in the English dubs, as well,

01:10:21.980 --> 01:10:23.620
because like a lot of the English dubs

01:10:23.620 --> 01:10:26.070
are also overseen by the
original directors and producers.

01:10:26.070 --> 01:10:28.600
So it's like, I feel like
they're finally starting

01:10:28.600 --> 01:10:30.370
to realize like, "Oh,
we can't just get anyone

01:10:30.370 --> 01:10:32.800
who can speak moderately good English.

01:10:32.800 --> 01:10:34.580
If we need an American role,

01:10:34.580 --> 01:10:37.020
we need to get an
American speaking person."

01:10:37.020 --> 01:10:40.840
- Yeah, I did an American
voice for a film.

01:10:40.840 --> 01:10:43.020
The one that like Charlie Cr1TiKaL is in?

01:10:43.020 --> 01:10:43.881
- Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:10:43.881 --> 01:10:45.585
I was like the killer,
but I wasn't credited!

01:10:45.585 --> 01:10:48.160
- You weren't credited?
- Oh really?

01:10:48.160 --> 01:10:48.993
- I think they forgot.

01:10:48.993 --> 01:10:50.931
I had to tell them, seriously.

01:10:50.931 --> 01:10:51.790
- Oh my god.

01:10:51.790 --> 01:10:54.810
- So yeah, I was the voice
of their like killer.

01:10:54.810 --> 01:10:55.643
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:10:55.643 --> 01:10:59.393
- And it's this like really
raspy, deep, scary voice.

01:10:59.393 --> 01:11:00.330
- Like American accent.

01:11:00.330 --> 01:11:02.170
- And they were like,
"We want you to do..."

01:11:02.170 --> 01:11:03.975
And I'm sitting there, I
remember that we were having the,

01:11:03.975 --> 01:11:05.180
I was having the call with the people

01:11:05.180 --> 01:11:06.710
who were making this film,

01:11:06.710 --> 01:11:08.180
and they were telling me about this role.

01:11:08.180 --> 01:11:10.640
And then this has gone
on for like half an hour

01:11:10.640 --> 01:11:14.230
and they mentioned, "Oh
yeah, he's American."

01:11:14.230 --> 01:11:16.990
And then at the end of it, I
was like, "So like the accent,

01:11:16.990 --> 01:11:19.479
I don't know if you
noticed, I'm not American."

01:11:19.479 --> 01:11:21.108
(all laughing)

01:11:21.108 --> 01:11:22.626
I was like, "So what'd you want me to do?"

01:11:22.626 --> 01:11:24.530
And they're like, "Well,
he is an American.

01:11:24.530 --> 01:11:25.800
So could you do American?"

01:11:25.800 --> 01:11:28.662
And I'm like, "I can,
but it won't be good."

01:11:28.662 --> 01:11:29.850
- Right.
- So I did it.

01:11:29.850 --> 01:11:32.000
- I feel, though, your American accent

01:11:32.000 --> 01:11:33.690
is probably better than most, right?

01:11:33.690 --> 01:11:34.563
Because I feel, I don't know.

01:11:34.563 --> 01:11:36.330
- When I do deep voices it's easier,

01:11:36.330 --> 01:11:37.620
'cause the mouth shape is easier.

01:11:37.620 --> 01:11:39.587
But, it's still shit, it's still shit.

01:11:39.587 --> 01:11:41.359
- But I feel like--
- You would laugh at me.

01:11:41.359 --> 01:11:44.220
- But I feel like a lot of
British actors, for instance,

01:11:44.220 --> 01:11:47.470
are usually pretty good at
nailing the American accent.

01:11:47.470 --> 01:11:49.520
- There are so many British or just like,

01:11:50.480 --> 01:11:52.109
actors not from America
that you don't know

01:11:52.109 --> 01:11:53.940
aren't from America until it's outed.

01:11:53.940 --> 01:11:55.769
But then you switch, you
swap to the other way around

01:11:55.769 --> 01:11:58.670
with Americans doing like British accents.

01:11:58.670 --> 01:12:00.230
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Right, right.

01:12:00.230 --> 01:12:01.550
'Cause like how many people think,

01:12:01.550 --> 01:12:03.267
if they watch like "Batman"
for me instance, right?

01:12:03.267 --> 01:12:06.450
Like Christian Bale and Gary Oldman,

01:12:06.450 --> 01:12:08.030
are both not American.
- Yeah.

01:12:08.030 --> 01:12:09.050
- Christian Bale is Welsh, right?

01:12:09.050 --> 01:12:10.115
- Yeah Christian Bale is Welsh.

01:12:10.115 --> 01:12:10.948
- Wow.
- Right?

01:12:10.948 --> 01:12:12.390
- Yeah, I'm pretty sure
he was born in Wales.

01:12:12.390 --> 01:12:13.860
- And Gary Oldman is very British.

01:12:13.860 --> 01:12:16.110
So it's like, it's just
incredible to think

01:12:16.110 --> 01:12:17.771
that a lot of people just don't know.

01:12:17.771 --> 01:12:19.964
- Chris Hemsworth, as
well, is like an Aussie.

01:12:19.964 --> 01:12:21.278
- Yeah, Chris Hemsworth is an Australian.

01:12:21.278 --> 01:12:22.887
- He's the most fucking
Aussie-guy I've ever seen.

01:12:22.887 --> 01:12:23.830
- But he nails the American accent.

01:12:23.830 --> 01:12:25.342
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:12:25.342 --> 01:12:27.310
- I think, yeah, 'cause they teach,

01:12:27.310 --> 01:12:29.380
they train British actors
different to American,

01:12:29.380 --> 01:12:31.480
it's a lot different
ways of learning acting.

01:12:31.480 --> 01:12:32.863
So I feel like that has
a lot to do with it.

01:12:32.863 --> 01:12:34.987
Because like British are more
focused on like stage acting.

01:12:34.987 --> 01:12:36.337
- Right!
- Right.

01:12:36.337 --> 01:12:37.255
- And learning that aspect of it.

01:12:37.255 --> 01:12:38.213
- Like theater training?
- Yeah, yeah.

01:12:38.213 --> 01:12:39.430
And being more like classically trained.

01:12:39.430 --> 01:12:41.380
So it's a bit different, I don't know.

01:12:41.380 --> 01:12:44.330
- And I also feel like if
you're going into acting,

01:12:44.330 --> 01:12:46.518
you kind of need to learn
how to do an American accent

01:12:46.518 --> 01:12:49.460
because that's where most
films are made, right?

01:12:49.460 --> 01:12:51.524
But it's just not the
same, the other way round.

01:12:51.524 --> 01:12:52.357
- True.
- I hate doing

01:12:52.357 --> 01:12:53.423
an American accent.

01:12:53.423 --> 01:12:54.930
You always have to do it for things.

01:12:54.930 --> 01:12:55.763
It sucks, I hate it.

01:12:55.763 --> 01:12:57.588
Just let me use my British accent.

01:12:57.588 --> 01:13:00.131
- Right, just give me like
an Australian character?

01:13:00.131 --> 01:13:02.822
- I've never seen an
Australian character before.

01:13:02.822 --> 01:13:04.080
- No, me neither.

01:13:04.080 --> 01:13:05.730
Wait, the one time where I was like,

01:13:05.730 --> 01:13:07.919
oo, I might have a chance
is like, what was it?

01:13:07.919 --> 01:13:11.000
"The Free," like was it a movie?

01:13:11.000 --> 01:13:12.531
Or like season two.
- Oh yeah!

01:13:12.531 --> 01:13:15.575
- It was based in Sydney!
- Yeah, it was, it was.

01:13:15.575 --> 01:13:19.040
- And so I was like, I was
waiting for that phone call.

01:13:19.040 --> 01:13:21.230
Being like-
- Joey finally made it.

01:13:21.230 --> 01:13:23.521
- Is it my time to shine?
- My time to shine.

01:13:23.521 --> 01:13:25.270
- My time to shine in
the Australian accent?

01:13:25.270 --> 01:13:26.103
Never happened.

01:13:26.103 --> 01:13:26.936
- They did it, did they speak,

01:13:26.936 --> 01:13:28.041
they spoke English in it, right?

01:13:28.041 --> 01:13:28.874
And it was like terrible.

01:13:28.874 --> 01:13:31.513
- Yeah, but they get hired
non-Australian actors

01:13:31.513 --> 01:13:33.685
and actresses, so I'm like-
- Yeah.

01:13:33.685 --> 01:13:35.608
- Missed opportunity there.
- I'm right here.

01:13:35.608 --> 01:13:36.441
- Yeah.
- I'm right here.

01:13:36.441 --> 01:13:37.581
- I'm literally right here.

01:13:37.581 --> 01:13:39.157
Me and Shu are right here.

01:13:39.157 --> 01:13:40.432
- Two people right here.

01:13:40.432 --> 01:13:41.730
- What does the author like?
- Just hit up

01:13:41.730 --> 01:13:42.960
that fucking Saturday school.

01:13:42.960 --> 01:13:43.801
- Yeah, exactly!

01:13:43.801 --> 01:13:45.543
(laughing drowns out Garnt)

01:13:45.543 --> 01:13:48.440
- What do you think of
the bad English in anime,

01:13:48.440 --> 01:13:51.470
as somebody--
- Well,

01:13:51.470 --> 01:13:54.720
I know people who who've been
asked to like talk in English

01:13:54.720 --> 01:13:56.470
when they're not like,
you know that talented.

01:13:56.470 --> 01:13:58.510
- Is the director's just
like, "You should just do it."

01:13:58.510 --> 01:14:00.513
- Yeah, they kind of like, well,

01:14:00.513 --> 01:14:03.180
they're like try your best, but you know.

01:14:03.180 --> 01:14:06.370
And obviously the actors
are trying their best.

01:14:06.370 --> 01:14:07.203
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:14:07.203 --> 01:14:09.294
- I just feel like it's
an unfortunate situation.

01:14:09.294 --> 01:14:10.177
- Yeah, yeah.

01:14:10.177 --> 01:14:11.485
- It's just kind of like, aw.

01:14:11.485 --> 01:14:13.073
I guess they had to, but.

01:14:13.073 --> 01:14:16.720
- Like a lot of my friends
ask me how to pronounce stuff.

01:14:16.720 --> 01:14:18.490
'Cause they're like, I don't know how,

01:14:18.490 --> 01:14:21.590
like, they pronounce the
sentence and stuff like that.

01:14:21.590 --> 01:14:23.870
So yeah I think it's just really hard

01:14:23.870 --> 01:14:25.770
for them to pronounce something

01:14:25.770 --> 01:14:27.180
that they're not used to pronouncing.

01:14:27.180 --> 01:14:28.650
- Do they ever worry
about how it's perceived

01:14:28.650 --> 01:14:30.350
by like a foreign fans?

01:14:30.350 --> 01:14:31.183
- Yeah, they do.

01:14:31.183 --> 01:14:33.320
They're like, you know, I tried my best,

01:14:33.320 --> 01:14:35.955
but it's like, I don't
think it sounds like native.

01:14:35.955 --> 01:14:36.788
- Aw.

01:14:37.920 --> 01:14:40.975
- I feel bad laughing at
the "Kuroko" no Basuke.

01:14:40.975 --> 01:14:43.087
- What the lunchtime rush one?

01:14:43.087 --> 01:14:45.860
- "Kuroko" no Basuke
when they go to America.

01:14:45.860 --> 01:14:47.146
- Oh yeah, they go to America!

01:14:47.146 --> 01:14:48.270
I completely forgot.

01:14:48.270 --> 01:14:50.510
- And everyone's American,
but everyone's Japanese.

01:14:50.510 --> 01:14:52.912
Like it's, it's a trip.

01:14:52.912 --> 01:14:54.687
- Well, I mean, it's like the English

01:14:54.687 --> 01:14:56.320
in "Devilman Crybaby," as well, right?

01:14:56.320 --> 01:14:57.601
- Oh yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:14:57.601 --> 01:15:00.371
- And I have to do (speaking
in Japanese) next to that guy.

01:15:00.371 --> 01:15:01.390
- Oh really?
- Yeah.

01:15:01.390 --> 01:15:03.280
- It was Murase Ayumu.

01:15:03.280 --> 01:15:04.113
- Oh yeah.

01:15:04.113 --> 01:15:05.363
- And it's like, yeah, I mean-

01:15:05.363 --> 01:15:08.154
- I mean, it's not a
win, no one wins there.

01:15:08.154 --> 01:15:09.690
- Well yeah, no one wins.

01:15:09.690 --> 01:15:12.440
I mean like his English was
probably the most decent

01:15:12.440 --> 01:15:13.610
out of like all the other actors.

01:15:13.610 --> 01:15:16.260
But like I had the exact
same thing like during break,

01:15:16.260 --> 01:15:18.400
like all the actors were
coming up to me being like,

01:15:18.400 --> 01:15:19.233
how do you pronounce this?

01:15:19.233 --> 01:15:21.754
Or like, how do I make
this sound as fluent

01:15:21.754 --> 01:15:23.950
and like naturally speaking as possible?

01:15:23.950 --> 01:15:25.100
And I'm just like, dude you're
asking the wrong person.

01:15:25.100 --> 01:15:26.870
This is set in New York.

01:15:26.870 --> 01:15:29.328
I'm not even doing the accent correctly.

01:15:29.328 --> 01:15:31.550
Why are you asking me?

01:15:31.550 --> 01:15:33.893
Like, I'm struggling to say the letter R.

01:15:34.759 --> 01:15:37.010
- You should've been
like, "I'm walkin' here."

01:15:37.010 --> 01:15:38.640
- "I'm walkin' here!"
- Just say that.

01:15:38.640 --> 01:15:39.640
That's what everyone says.

01:15:39.640 --> 01:15:41.040
That's the meme, that's the meme.

01:15:41.040 --> 01:15:43.460
- Just give him a copy of
every Martin Scorsese film.

01:15:43.460 --> 01:15:45.121
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:15:45.121 --> 01:15:46.090
- God.
- Jesus.

01:15:46.090 --> 01:15:47.840
- Have you ever been recognized

01:15:47.840 --> 01:15:49.640
in Japan for your voice work?

01:15:49.640 --> 01:15:50.707
Like someone's spot on the street is like,

01:15:50.707 --> 01:15:51.540
"Oh my god, I know you."

01:15:51.540 --> 01:15:53.810
- Oh, I haven't had that before,

01:15:53.810 --> 01:15:56.627
but I've had someone
ask me like at a cafe,

01:15:56.627 --> 01:15:58.290
like when I was checking out,

01:15:58.290 --> 01:16:01.800
I've had someone ask me if
I was a voice actor and-

01:16:01.800 --> 01:16:02.633
- What just randomly?

01:16:02.633 --> 01:16:03.590
- Yeah, just randomly.

01:16:03.590 --> 01:16:05.798
- They could just feel the
voice acting aura from you.

01:16:05.798 --> 01:16:06.631
- Maybe?

01:16:06.631 --> 01:16:07.477
I don't know, like, yeah.

01:16:07.477 --> 01:16:11.880
And so like, it was like a young male guy

01:16:11.880 --> 01:16:13.763
and he was like, yeah, like,

01:16:14.727 --> 01:16:16.580
"Do you by any chance to do voice acting?"

01:16:16.580 --> 01:16:17.413
And I'm like-

01:16:17.413 --> 01:16:19.023
- Is that like a pickup line in Japan?

01:16:20.040 --> 01:16:21.622
Bro, that voice got me acting up.

01:16:21.622 --> 01:16:23.622
- Are you a voice actor?

01:16:24.630 --> 01:16:26.280
- I'm about to senpai your voice.

01:16:29.417 --> 01:16:31.354
- "My Queen, are you the voice actor?"

01:16:31.354 --> 01:16:32.405
- "My Queen, do you happen
to be a voice actor?"

01:16:32.405 --> 01:16:36.137
- Says one word, "My Queen,
I will simp for you."

01:16:37.425 --> 01:16:39.703
- Did you go to the checkout and say,

01:16:39.703 --> 01:16:41.070
like it in a voice actor way?

01:16:41.070 --> 01:16:42.854
Did you start barking, or?

01:16:42.854 --> 01:16:43.687
You're a cat?

01:16:43.687 --> 01:16:44.556
- No, or maybe did I?

01:16:44.556 --> 01:16:45.389
I don't know, maybe I did.

01:16:45.389 --> 01:16:47.140
- Give like the anime reaction lines.

01:16:47.140 --> 01:16:47.973
Like, eh?

01:16:49.077 --> 01:16:52.960
- Hontouni?
(all laughing)

01:16:52.960 --> 01:16:53.978
- You can have a point card.

01:16:53.978 --> 01:16:54.811
Hontouni!

01:16:56.430 --> 01:16:58.570
- So, for like everyone watching,

01:16:58.570 --> 01:17:02.160
who maybe want, aspires to
be a voice actor or actress,

01:17:02.160 --> 01:17:04.840
what do you think it takes to be one

01:17:04.840 --> 01:17:06.290
professionally in Japan?

01:17:06.290 --> 01:17:07.970
- I think it's like,

01:17:07.970 --> 01:17:10.310
obviously you need like
your acting skills,

01:17:10.310 --> 01:17:12.300
but I think it's more like
being able to communicate

01:17:12.300 --> 01:17:15.452
with the people around you and like, yeah.

01:17:15.452 --> 01:17:17.880
Like, 'cause if you have a manager,

01:17:17.880 --> 01:17:20.260
then you have, you have to
be in good relationships

01:17:20.260 --> 01:17:21.093
with your manager

01:17:21.093 --> 01:17:24.580
because they're the ones
picking who to push forward

01:17:24.580 --> 01:17:26.450
for the audition and
stuff like that, right.

01:17:26.450 --> 01:17:30.460
And you'll have to be
like doing good with,

01:17:30.460 --> 01:17:32.157
the voice actors around you

01:17:32.157 --> 01:17:35.632
and your senpais and yeah, I
think that's really important.

01:17:35.632 --> 01:17:37.103
- So it's just social politics, isn't it?

01:17:37.103 --> 01:17:37.936
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:17:37.936 --> 01:17:38.780
- That's how it always is, though.

01:17:38.780 --> 01:17:41.390
Like the entertainment industry
is always who you know,

01:17:41.390 --> 01:17:42.641
and who you're friends with, right?

01:17:42.641 --> 01:17:43.725
It's a bit unfortunate.

01:17:43.725 --> 01:17:46.160
I mean, even YouTubing
is like that, right?

01:17:46.160 --> 01:17:46.993
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- True, true.

01:17:46.993 --> 01:17:47.826
- It's who you're friends with, you know?

01:17:47.826 --> 01:17:48.730
- I feel that's just like,

01:17:48.730 --> 01:17:50.090
but I feel especially like

01:17:50.090 --> 01:17:53.470
that on top of how already
socially, politically,

01:17:53.470 --> 01:17:56.436
like charged, I guess
Japan is just in general.

01:17:56.436 --> 01:17:57.750
- [Shu] Yeah, mm hm.

01:17:57.750 --> 01:18:00.240
You have (speaking in Japanese)
and all that kind of stuff

01:18:00.240 --> 01:18:02.122
on top of, like-
- It's so hard.

01:18:02.122 --> 01:18:02.955
- In the entertainment industry.

01:18:02.955 --> 01:18:04.440
- Yeah, I'm always like,

01:18:04.440 --> 01:18:07.280
'cause like, even towards
your senpai, right.

